<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Buildmax beats listing forecast by 45 pct.</title>
<headline>Buildmax beats listing forecast by 45 pct.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		23.6	  vs 19.3</p>
<p>    - attrib		  23.6	  vs 19.3</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 7.9	   vs nil</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   7.16	  vs 4.06</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   9.84	  vs 4.61</p>
<p>    Tax			 2.68	  vs 0.56</p>
<p>    Interest		  0.85 gain   vs 1.05</p>
<p>    Turnover		  114.42	vs 75.74</p>
<p>Full name: Buildmax Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said they would be awarding capitalisation shares to shareholders in the books of the company on July 18 in the ratio that 7.9 cents holds to the firm's share price at the close averaged with the four prior trading days. Shareholders can instead elect to receive the dividend.</p>
<p>They said that the outlook for the remainder of the 15 month period to end June continues to remain positive. Pro-active organic growth and focussed acquisitions will continue to be the driving force for the firm. A number of new business opportunities are being explored, they said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
